// Test: error.overloads-disagree-on-returning-a-value-at-all
function emit(flag bool)
	print("flag {flag}")
end 'emit'

function emit(tag int) returns String
	return "tag{tag}"
end 'emit'

function main() returns ExitCode
	emit(true)
	return 0 as ExitCode
end 'main'
---
CompilerError:
error E2015: <fragment>:11:2: the overloads of 'emit' do not agree on their return type ('String' and 'void'), and this call needed the one they disagree about. A call's result type is fixed while its file is parsed, from a whole-program index that records one return type per NAME, so only a difference between plain scalars can be corrected once the overload is known. Make the overloads return the same type
